<p>Use this function to add background numbers when printing confidential 
 documents, for example.<br/>
An individual watermark number is printed on each copy. Recording the number 
 to be distributed among other users can prevent unauthorized copies.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Background Numbering</span> 
 check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span> 
 to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Background Numbering Details</span> 
 dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Specify the size, density, and color from <span class="Term-Soft">Size:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Density:</span> and 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Color:</span>.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent"><span class="Term-Soft">Color:</span> 
 is available only for color printers.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="6">
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Start Number:</span> 
 box, enter the start number for numbering.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
